---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const editorApi = [
  [
    'commands',
    'CommandsOf<T> & CoreCommands',
    'Every command from every extension you passed in, typed.',
  ],
  [
    'can',
    'CommandsOf<T> & CoreCommands',
    'The same commands, returning what they would return and changing nothing. For disabling a button before it is pressed.',
  ],
  [
    'isActive(name, attrs?)',
    'boolean',
    'Is this mark on, or is the caret inside a node of this type? Marks are looked up first.',
  ],
  [
    'batch(run)',
    'boolean',
    'Run several commands as one undo step. Rolls back entirely if any returns false.',
  ],
  ['getJSON()', 'DocNode', 'The document as plain JSON. No engine types.'],
  ['getHTML()', 'string', 'Serialised HTML, through the same security gate as rendering.'],
  ['getText()', 'string', 'Block-separated plain text.'],
  ['setContent(content)', 'void', 'Replace the document with JSON or an HTML string.'],
  ['selection', 'Selection', 'Current from, to, anchor, head and empty.'],
  ['editable / setEditable(v)', 'boolean / void', 'Read-only mode.'],
  [
    'on(event, fn)',
    '() => void',
    "'change' | 'focus' | 'blur' | 'selectionChange'. Returns its own unsubscribe.",
  ],
  ['extensionState(name)', 'S | undefined', 'What a stateful extension is currently holding.'],
  [
    'mount(element)',
    'void',
    'Attach to the DOM. Or pass `element` to createEditor and skip it.',
  ],
  ['destroy()', 'void', 'Detach and clean up.'],
  [
    'unsafe',
    '{ view, state, schema }',
    'Raw engine. Unstable, outside semver · needing it is a gap in the API above.',
  ],
]

const options = [
  [
    'extensions',
    'T',
    'Required. The feature list · it decides the schema, the keymap and the type of `commands`.',
  ],
  [
    'content',
    'DocNode | string',
    'JSON or HTML. Anything the schema cannot hold is dropped on the way in. Parsing an HTML string needs a DOM · JSON and `fromMarkdown` output do not.',
  ],
  ['element', 'HTMLElement', 'Mount here immediately, instead of calling `mount` later.'],
  ['editable', 'boolean', 'Defaults to true.'],
  ['autofocus', "boolean | 'start' | 'end'", 'Where to put the caret on mount.'],
]

const coreCommands = [
  ['select(range)', 'Range | Pos', 'Move the selection.'],
  [
    'insert(content, at?)',
    'DocNode | DocNode[] | string',
    'Insert at a position, or at the caret.',
  ],
  ['replace(range, content)', 'Range, content', 'Swap a range for something else.'],
  ['remove(range?)', 'Range?', 'Delete a range, or the selection.'],
  ['moveBlock(from, to)', 'Pos, Pos', 'Move a whole block · what a drag does.'],
  ['focus()', '—', 'Put the caret back.'],
]

const ctxApi = [
  ['doc / selection', 'The document and where the caret is.'],
  ['hasMark(name, attrs?)', 'True if the mark covers the whole selection.'],
  ['inNode(name, attrs?)', 'True if the selection sits inside such a node.'],
  ['addMark / removeMark / toggleMark', 'Marks across a range.'],
  ['setBlockType(name, attrs?)', 'Turn the block into another type.'],
  ['wrapIn(name, attrs?) / lift()', 'Wrap the selection, or unwrap it.'],
  ['insert / replace / delete / select', 'The same primitives the core commands expose.'],
  ['mark()', 'A PosMarker. Map positions through changes made after this point.'],
]
---

<Docs
  title="API · Matra docs"
  description="The editor object, the core commands, and the command context, in one page."
  section="Reference"
  heading="API"
>
  <p>
    Everything public, on one page. No engine type appears in any signature here · that is the
    contract, not a coincidence.
  </p>

  <h2>createEditor(options)</h2>
  <div class="api">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          options.map(([name, type, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono n">{name}</td>
              <td class="mono t">{type}</td>
              <td class="d">{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Editor</h2>
  <div class="api">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Returns</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          editorApi.map(([name, type, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono n">{name}</td>
              <td class="mono t">{type}</td>
              <td class="d">{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Core commands</h2>
  <p>Always present, whatever extensions you loaded. Every one returns a boolean.</p>
  <div class="api">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Arguments</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          coreCommands.map(([name, args, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="mono n">{name}</td>
              <td class="mono t">{args}</td>
              <td class="d">{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    A command never throws. Positions that are not finite integers inside the document return
    false · <code>NaN</code> included, which slips past naive range checks because both
    <code>NaN &lt; 0</code> and <code>NaN &gt; size</code> are false.
  </div>

  <h2>Ctx · what a command receives</h2>
  <div class="api">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        {
          ctxApi.map(([name, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <>
                <td class="mono n">{name}</td>
                <td class="d">{note}</td>
              </>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What an extension may declare</h2>
  <div class="api">
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">commands</td><td class="d"
            >Plain functions of <code>(ctx, …args) =&gt; boolean</code>. Their types land on <code
              >editor.commands</code
            > and <code>editor.can</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">keys</td><td class="d"
            >A binding to a command name or a function · <code
              >&#123; 'Mod-Shift-S': 'toggleSpoiler' &#125;</code
            >. A binding that returns false lets the next one try.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">inputRules</td><td class="d"
            >A RegExp on the text before the caret and a handler. One undo step each.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">attributes</td><td class="d"
            >Attributes added to nodes and marks defined elsewhere, rendered and parsed.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">handlePaste · handleDrop</td><td class="d"
            >Claim a paste or a drop before the editor parses it. Return true to keep it.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">filterChange</td><td class="d"
            >Veto a change before it lands. Nothing is applied, recorded or redrawn when it
            returns false.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">decorations</td><td class="d"
            >Draw over the document: inline attributes, node attributes, widgets. Never in the
            document.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">state</td><td class="d"
            ><code>init</code> and <code>apply</code>, reduced on every transaction · read with <code
              >editor.extensionState(name)</code
            >.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">nodeViews</td><td class="d"
            >Render nodes defined elsewhere with your own DOM, keyed by node name.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">onCreate · onChange · onDestroy</td><td class="d"
            >Lifecycle, each handed the editor. <code>onCreate</code> runs when the editor mounts.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">priority</td><td class="d"
            >Load order. Higher loads first; a later binding for the same key wins.</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="mono n">nodes · marks</td><td class="d"
            >A node declares <code>content</code>, <code>group</code>, <code>attrs</code>, <code
              >parseDOM</code
            >, <code>toDOM</code>, <code>nodeView</code>, <code>listItem</code>, <code
              >marks</code
            >, <code>code</code>; a mark declares <code>inclusive</code>, <code>excludes</code>, <code
              >parseDOM</code
            >, <code>toDOM</code>.</td
          ></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Types worth knowing</h2>
  <pre><code>type Pos = number &amp; &#123; readonly __pos: unique symbol &#125;
type Range = &#123; from: Pos; to: Pos &#125;

interface DocNode &#123;
  type: string
  attrs?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;
  content?: DocNode[]
  text?: string
  marks?: DocMark[]
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>Pos</code> is branded so a raw number cannot be passed by accident. Cast at the boundary
    where you genuinely know the number is a position.
  </p>

  <h2>Writing a position down</h2>
  <pre><code>import &#123; pos, range &#125; from '@matrajs/core'

pos(0)         // number -> Pos
range(1, 6)    // (number, number) -> Range</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>Pos</code> is branded so that arithmetic on one does not typecheck · these are how you write
    a literal without a cast. Not for carrying a position across an <code>await</code>: that is <code
      >ctx.mark()</code
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Functions that need no editor</h2>
  <pre><code>import &#123; toMarkdown, fromMarkdown, tableOfContents, assignIds &#125; from '@matrajs/core'

toMarkdown(doc)          // DocNode  -> string
fromMarkdown(source)     // string   -> DocNode
tableOfContents(doc)     // DocNode  -> TocEntry[]
assignIds(doc, options)  // DocNode  -> DocNode with stable block ids</code></pre>
  <p>None of these touches the DOM, so all four run on a server.</p>

  <style>
    .api {
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 0 0 18px;
    }
    .api table {
      border-collapse: collapse;
      width: 100%;
      font-size: 13.5px;
    }
    .api td,
    .api th {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 9px 12px;
      background-image: var(--dash-h);
      background-size: 100% 1px;
      background-position: 0 100%;
      background-repeat: no-repeat;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .api th {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-faint);
      font-weight: 400;
    }
    .api td.n {
      white-space: nowrap;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .api td.t {
      white-space: nowrap;
      color: var(--indigo);
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .api td.d {
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }
  </style>
</Docs>
